                            Preamble

  The GNU Affero General Public License is a free, copyleft license for
software and other kinds of works, specifically designed to ensure
cooperation with the community in the case of network server software.

  The licenses for most software and other practical works are designed
to take away your freedom to share and change the works.  By contrast,
our General Public Licenses are intended to guarantee your freedom to
share and change all versions of a program--to make sure it remains free
software for all its users.

  This license, similar to the GNU General Public License, is intended
to guarantee your freedom to share and change free works--to make sure the
work remains free for all its users.

  When we speak of free software, we are referring to freedom, not
price.  Our General Public Licenses are designed to make sure that you
have the freedom to distribute copies of free software (and charge for
this service if you wish), that you receive source code or can get it
if you want it, that you can change the software or use pieces of it
in new free programs, and that you know you can do these things.

  To protect your rights, a license will grant you the rights to use,
copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
copies of the work, and to grant recipients of the work the rights
that are granted by this license.

  For the implementation of this license, we recommend that you
consider using the GPL version 3 or later as the license for a copy
of the program.  If you can, you should choose the license that
provides your rights with the most protection against being enjoined
from exercising those rights.

  The GNU Affero General Public License addresses how to deal with
the possibility of a work being used as a server-side application
without providing the source code to the users of that application.

  By contrast, the GNU General Public License is a conventional
copyleft license that is designed to prohibit you from sharing or
changing it.  If you modified this file, you would not be able to use
it in any commercial application.

  The GNU Affero General Public License is designed to take this
further and requires the same copyleft that would apply if the work
were made available to everyone.  This ensures that a larger community
can benefit from this work.

  An additional term to the GNU Affero General Public License allows
for linking or combining a work with other work not covered by this
license.  The combination is made available under the terms of this
license, and the sections of this license will be relevant to the
combination if the work is used outside of the network.

  A copyright notice and a notice of attribution from the work
must accompany all copies of the licensed work or derivative
works.

