  4. Conveying Verbatim Copies.

    You may convey verbatim copies of the Program's source code as you
receive it, in any medium, provided that you conspicuously and
appropriately publish on each copy an appropriate copyright notice;
keep intact all notices stating that this License and any
non-permissive terms added in accord with section 7 apply to the code;
keep intact all notices of absence of any warranty; and give all
recipients a copy of this License along with the Program.

    You may charge a fee for the physical act of transferring a copy,
and you may at your discretion offer warranty protection in exchange
for a fee.

  5. Conveying Modified Copies.

    You may convey a work based on the Program, or the modifications to
produce it from the Program, in the form of source code under the
terms of section 4, provided that you also meet all of these conditions:

    a) The work must be modified by changing or replacing it, so that it
is based on the Program and can be changed by laws relating to
copyright, and the recipient of the original work receives a copy of
this License.

    b) If you can communicate with a recipient of the work, or for any
reason do not allow access to the source code of the work, you must
convey the source code of that work by some means, in accordance with
this License.  You may not impose any additional terms or restrictions
on the recipients of the source code from the work.  The source code
may not be distributed through any website, news group, or
mailing list, unless these sites are closed to the public.

    c) You must convey all source code, including any differences
between the original work and the modified work, as well as the
scripts used to control compilation and installation of the modified
work, under the terms of this License.  The difference between the
original work and the modified work is material, but not necessarily
a complete difference.

    d) If the work is integrated with a network server, you must provide
the source code to the server as well as the work.  This is not always
required by law, but is demanded by the terms of this License to ensure
that a community develops this work.

  6. Conveying Non-Source Form.

    You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of section 4 and section 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable source code under the terms of this License, in one
of these ways:

    a) Convey the object code in, or with, a physical product (including
a physical distribution medium), accompanied by the information
required by section 4 and section 5 on a durable physical medium
customarily used for software interchange.

    b) Convey the object code in, or with, a written offer, with
access to copy the source code from a public place at no charge for
at least three years, to give any recipient the object code a copy
of the source code for at least three years after the object code
was transferred to the recipient.

    c) Convey the object code by installing, releasing, or promoting
the object code and the source code on a public website for no charge,
with access to copy the source code from that website by the user,
at least three years after the date on which you last exercise
your rights under this License on the covered work.

